      "name": "Sabarmati Ashram",
      "city": "Ahmedabad",
      "description": "Historic ashram on the banks of the Sabarmati River that served as Mahatma Gandhi's residence during India's freedom movement. Features simple cottages, prayer grounds, and museum galleries offering insight into Gandhi's philosophy of truth, simplicity, and non-violence.",
      "hours": "10:00 AM – 6:00 PM",
      "entry_fee": "Free",
      "recommended_duration": null,
      "source_files": [
